  "scope": "For explicit finite cyclic products and an exact labelled ordered square of a three-element support, choose binary odd powers solely from R using certified rational Machin/Taylor centres and a squared-norm threshold. The bank keeps the exact minimum number of character readings and separates distinct supports in the fibre by at least two in the sup norm of unweighted unitary character sums. The typed decoder, with checked rational precision parameters, uniquely recovers a support from coordinatewise absolute error epsilon<1, and returns at most one candidate on every typed input. Candidate generation uses at most twenty representatives. Worst-case odd search can inspect half the binary primary order; no polynomial bit complexity, noisy square, universal Python/JSON equivalence, or raw-parser verification is claimed.",
